 "literal": "Painting time stick not-seeing eye-itself like lover's fault I-see-not seen time.",
 "translation": "Like the eye that cannot see the kohl-stick when being painted, I cannot see my lover's faults when I look at him.",
 "modern": "கண்ணுக்கு மை தீட்டும்போது அந்த மைத்தீட்டும் குச்சியை கண் பார்க்க முடியாதது போல, என் தலைவனை நான் நேரில் பார்க்கும் போது அவனுடைய தவறுகளை என்னால் காண முடிவதில்லை.",
 "explanation": "The speaker compares her inability to stay angry at her lover to an eye being painted with kohl. Just as the eye cannot see the stick applying the makeup because it is too close, she cannot see her lover's faults when he is right in front of her. She only remembers his flaws and feels angry when he is away, but his presence blinds her to everything except her love for him.",
